# /etc/inittab — Variant A: busybox init + OpenRC with a two-service runlevel.
#
# PID 1 is busybox. OpenRC is not the init here, it is a service manager with
# dependency ordering that busybox init lacks. Two services, and that is the
# whole process table: init, velad, wpa_supplicant.
#
# If /usr/sbin/velad is missing (a build before P4), we start a shell on the
# console rather than respawning a binary that does not exist — a respawn loop
# with no console is indistinguishable from a dead device.

::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/vela-boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

# The daemon owns the panel, touch, audio, wake word, network client and OTA.
# It must be PID-owned here so a crash is reaped and reported, not ignored.
::respawn:/usr/sbin/velad

# Serial console, if one is wired. `askfirst` means it does not steal the tty.
ttyMT0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L ttyMT0 921600 vt100
::askfirst:-/bin/sh

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::restart:/sbin/init
